mode: "100644"
text: "# Post Craft — writing the posts\n\nA thread is read post by post. Each one is its own unit on the screen, so each has to be written\nas one — not as a sentence sliced from a paragraph.\n\n## The opener formula\n\nPost 1 does two jobs in one or two lines: **hook + promise.**\n\n- **Hook** — a real mechanism from `hook-writer` (curiosity, stakes, specificity, contrarian,\n  story). Stop the scroll.\n- **Promise** — tell the reader what they'll get by staying (\"here's exactly how,\" \"7 lessons from\n  it,\" \"the full story\").\n\nIt must also **stand alone as a strong post**, because the opener is what people reshare — and the\nreshare is how the thread reaches new people. If post 1 only makes sense as setup for post 2, it's\ntoo weak.\n\nOpener shapes (rewrite in voice):\n- *Specificity + promise:* \"We deleted 80% of our features and revenue went up. Here's what we\n  learned 🧵\"\n- *Stakes + promise:* \"This one mistake cost us our biggest customer. The 5 lessons so you avoid\n  it:\"\n- *Story open:* \"Two years ago we almost shut down. Here's the 30 days that saved us 👇\"\n\n## Each post is a standalone unit\n\n- **Front-load the point.** The first line of every post is what shows in the timeline — lead with\n  it, no warm-up.\n- **One beat per post.** One step, one lesson, one scene.\n- **Readable within the post.** Use line breaks for scannability; don't write a wall.\n\n## Length discipline\n\n- X: **280 characters per post** (longer with Premium, but short travels and reads better). Don't\n  split a sentence awkwardly across posts; end posts on clean breaks.\n- Keep each post tight — a thread is a series of punches, not paragraphs.\n\n## Transitions and momentum\n\n- Number posts (\"3/\" or \"3/9\") where it helps orientation and signals more is coming.\n- Use light forward pulls between posts (\"but here's the part that surprised us\") — without\n  withholding value for cheap.\n- Cut every filler post and every \"as I mentioned\" — momentum dies on throat-clearing.\n\n## The close + CTA\n\nThe final post:\n\n1. **Lands the payoff** — the lesson, the recap, the result. Don't trail off.\n2. **Makes one CTA**, in voice, matched to the goal:\n   - *Growth (X-native):* \"If this was useful, RT the first post so others see it 👇\" and/or \"I\n     write about {topic} — follow for more.\"\n   - *Traffic:* link to the full piece (often in a reply, since links can dampen reach).\n   - *Community:* \"What would you add?\"\n\n**One ask only.** The reshare-the-opener move is the highest-leverage growth CTA on X — it sends\nnew readers back to the top of the thread.\n\n## A quick post-by-post check\n\nFor each post ask: does it **front-load**, deliver **one beat**, stay **in voice**, fit the\n**limit**, and **pull forward**? If a post fails any, fix it. If it adds nothing, delete it.\n"
